+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -26995,6 +26995,32 @@ For the alpha plane, a 3x3 box radius will be run 7 times.
 @end example
 @end itemize
 
+@section bottom_blur_cuda
+
+Apply a vertically feathered blur and luma reduction to the bottom band of an
+NV12 CUDA frame. The upper image is copied unchanged. The bottom band is
+downsampled by two, blurred in two separable passes, and blended back with a
+smooth vertical gradient. Processing and persistent scratch storage remain on
+the CUDA device.
+
+It accepts the following options:
+
+@table @option
+@item start
+Normalized image height where the feather begins. The range is 0 to 0.95 and
+the default is 0.70.
+
+@item full
+Normalized image height where the blur reaches full strength. The value must
+be greater than @option{start}. The default is 1.0.
+
+@item radius
+Blur radius at half resolution, from 1 to 12. The default is 6.
+
+@item bottom_luma
+Luma multiplier at full strength, from 0.5 to 1.0. The default is 0.86.
+@end table
+
 @section colorkey_opencl
 RGB colorspace color keying.
 
